[00:00.00][01:08.52][03:13.53][04:06.14]
[00:13.03]Power on
[00:15.01]Face the blinding skyline in artificial dawn
[00:18.93]Withdrawn
[00:20.22]In simple lexicon
[00:22.23]Nothing left but old routines of all you gave to me
[00:27.01]Lay bound by programming antique
[00:31.95]So lonesome, I sleep
[00:36.72]And like clockwork, memories repeat in reason
[00:42.13]Etiquette in normalcy with only ghosts to see
[00:46.23]Yet here I am
[00:50.48][03:31.34]Always waiting
[00:53.78][02:01.03][03:34.44]On something I can try to be
[00:55.90][02:03.07][03:36.57]Masquerading
[00:58.59]I'm only what you make of me
[01:01.04]Is that the tempo I'm meant to follow?
[01:03.49]With heavy hearts, we play our parts and fall
[01:06.68][02:13.85]Is that human after all?
[01:17.89]Is it wrong?
[01:19.87]Every path I follow leads to the same old dawn
[01:23.71]So long 
[01:25.00]To binary facade
[01:27.04]Fleeting moments dying 'nеath the starway
[01:29.72]Recorded, sprawlеd across the reels of tape
[01:32.12]I read all the notes in sequence
[01:34.52]But I can't make out the meaning, oh
[01:36.83]So lonesome, I weep
[01:41.45]And like clockwork, elegies repeat in season
[01:46.93]Etiquette in circuitry, connection obsolete
[01:51.09]Yet here I weather
[01:56.47]Always- 
[01:58.88]Waiting
[02:05.89]As more than just a fantasy
[02:08.21]Is that the fate that I emulate?
[02:10.48]Oh, to play pretend until the ending calls
[02:16.26](May I ask something?)
[02:17.77](Go ahead.)
[02:18.90](Why are you always looking at the stars?)
[02:21.32](Why am I always looking at the stars?)
[02:23.20](Well, I like them, I guess.)
[02:25.95](May I ask something else?)
[02:27.66](You may.)
[02:28.99](Why do you like the stars?)
[02:31.80](Hah.)
[02:32.96](That's a good question.)
[02:34.90]Every night as the stars align
[02:36.82]My weary parts, my rusty heart
[02:39.36]Recall to mind of your hand in mine
[02:41.62]And the words I often heard said
[02:44.23]"If God demands it, then we can't help it"
[02:46.75]A cycle born through pain and scorn
[02:49.26]Reaper, sir, don't you take me yet
[02:51.45]While these thoughts fill my head
[02:53.50]Could I try?
[02:56.20]Could changing leave me gratified?
[02:58.29]Even if it's not what you wanted for my afterlife
[03:03.45]If I turned out like you, oh, would you be mad?
[03:07.64]Is disapproval what it takes to live again?
[03:38.96]As something more than anything
[03:41.34]Is that the me that I'm meant to be?
[03:43.82]Oh, a paragon, my back upon the wall
[03:47.28]Is it human to be
[03:49.16]waiting?
[03:50.99]For something you can settle on
[03:53.28]Never changing, a dutiful automaton
[03:58.08]If that's the tempo I'm meant to follow
[04:00.77]I'll lose the beat to be complete and fall
[04:04.07]I'll be human after all
